nk at hotel.\r\n\r\n Half day sightseeing at Kathmandu covering Swyambhunath Stupa (Monkey Temple) & Kathmandu Durbar Square.\r\n\r\n Dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\n Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\r\n\r\n26 Aug. 2022:\r\n\r\n Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n\r\n Drive from hotel to Kathmandu domestic airport via half day sightseeing at Kathmandu covering Pashupatinath Temple & Bauddhanath Stupa. (Flight to \r\n Pokhara) Flight time: 13.10 PM\r\n\r\n Pickup from Pokhara airport & drop at hotel.\r\n\r\n Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\n\r\n Dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\n Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.\r\n\r\n27 Aug. 2022:\r\n\r\n Morning breakfast at hotel\r\n\r\n Drive from hotel to Pokhara airport. (Flight to Jomsom)Flight time: 06:30 AM Approx\r\n\r\n Pickup from Jomsom airport drop at hotel. \r\n\r\n Drive from Jomsom to Muktinath Temple darshan by private Vehicle.\r\n\r\n Dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\n Overnight stay at hotel in Jomsom\r\n\r\n28 Aug. 2022:\r\n\r\n Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n\r\n Jomsom to Pokhara flight   (Flight to Pokhara) Flight time: 08:30 AM Approx\r\n\r\n Pickup from Pokhara airport and drop at hotel.\r\n\r\n Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\n\r\n Full day sightseeing at Pokhara covering Bindabashini Temple, Gupteshor Cave, Devi’s fall, Seti River, Fewa Lake & Peace Pagoda.\r\n\r\n Dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\n Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.\r\n\r\n29 Aug. 2022:\r\n\r\n Morning breakfast at hotel\r\n\r\n Drive from hotel to Pokhara airport. (Flight to Kathmandu)  Flight time: 12:55 PM\r\n\r\n Pickup from Kathmandu domestic airport drop at hotel. \r\n\r\n Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\n\r\n Dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\n Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\r\n\r\n30 Aug. 2022:\r\n\r\n Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n\r\n Drive from hotel to Kathmandu International Airport.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','Return Airfare\r\n\r\n Welcome soft drink.\r\n\r\n Airport pickup & drop with a/c Scorpio.\r\n\r\n 02 nights accommodation at respective hotel in Kathmandu with MAP Plan. \r\n\r\n 02 nights accommodation at respective hotel in Pokhara with MAP Plan. \r\n\r\n 01 nights accommodation at respective hotel in Jomsom with MAP Plan \r\n\r\n Kathmandu two half day sightseeing.\r\n\r\n Pokhara one full day sightseeing.\r\n\r\n KTM-PKR-KTM by flight\r\n\r\n PKR-JOMSOM-PKR by flight\r\n',' Monuments and museum entrance fees for above sightseeing places.\r\n\r\n Jomsom Permit charge.\r\n\r\n Anything which is not included in inclusions.','','2022-08-25','2022-08-30',1,0,0,'2022-07-22 16:22:16','2022-07-22 16:24:20'),(147,437,6,4,2,0,81200,22000,'Andaman','Destination : Andaman and Nicobar Islands\r\n\r\nPort Blair 1 Night / Havelock 2 Nights / Neil Island 1 Night / Port Blair 1 Night\r\n\r\nStart Date : 10 August, 2022\r\n\r\nTrip Duration : 5 Nights / 6 Days\r\n\r\nPax 4 Adults, 2 Children (4y, 6y)\r\n\r\nNationality : Indian\r\n\r\n1st Day (Wed 10th August) : Port Blair Arrival - Cellular Jail – Light & Sound Show\r\n\r\n• Arrival, Meet-Greet with our airport representative and Transfer to your booked hotel / resort\r\n\r\n• Evening, visit to historic Cellular Jail followed by Light & Sound Show\r\n\r\n• Please note, we will drop guests at the parking area near jail and guests must walk around 200 metre and return after completion of L&S show.\r\n\r\n• Guests must come out after visiting jail and re-enter for the L&S show, Guests can walk around the bay side in their free time\r\n.\r\n• L&S show timing is in between 1800hrs - 1900hrs subject to availability\r\n\r\n• The free time between jail visit & L&S show can be utilised in self-exploration of illuminated\r\n\r\n• Marina Park and the Sea shore area, evenings are pleasant and happening here.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Thu 11th August) : Port Blair to Havelock - Radha Nagar Beach\r\n\r\n• Pick up from hotel to Port Blair Jetty for your onward journey to Havelock\r\n\r\n• If you have morning ferry, ask hotel to provide Packed breakfast (Subject to hotel policy)\r\n\r\n• Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\n\r\n• Afternoon, Visit to Blue Flag certified “Radha Nagar Beach” for swim and relaxation.\r\n\r\n• Do not forget to carry changing clothes and towels\r\n\r\n• It’s not permitted to board vehicles with wet clothes, please cooperate.\r\n\r\n• Make your own choice …. You can opt for Scuba Diving/ Kayaking/ Candid Photography at additional cost, booking in advance is recommended though our \r\n local representative also can assist you.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Fri 12th August) : Havelock - Elephenta Beach\r\n\r\n• Morning, Breakfast and proceed for “Elephenta Beach” also known as Coral Beach.\r\n\r\n• Elephenta beach is popular for Snorkelling and other water-based activities such as Jet Ski ride, Banana Ride, Sea Walk.\r\n\r\n• Usually boat operators provide a 5-minute snorkelling experience complimentary, however the same cannot be guaranteed\r\n\r\n• You reach Elephenta beach via small 11 pax capacity sharing basis boat board at jetty\r\n\r\n• You will be allotted a time for boat a day before and you need to get ready accordingly\r\n\r\n• Do not forget to carry a water bottle, snacks and changing cloths.\r\n\r\n• Important: In case Elephenta Beach is not operational due to weather conditions OR COVID-19 reasons, we will provide a trip to “Kala Pathar Beach” \r\n OR We can refund the applicable amount.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Sat 13th August) : Havelock to Neil Island - Laxmanpura Beach, Bharatpura Beach & Natural Bridge\r\n\r\n• Morning, Breakfast & proceed to jetty for onward journey to Neil Island\r\n\r\n• Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\n\r\n• Afternoon, proceed to visit the following places:\r\n\r\n• Bharatpura Beach: The white sand and shallow water beach is popular for swim, relaxation, and water activities such as Snorkelling, Boat diving and \r\n boat tour.\r\n\r\n• Laxmanpura beach: The white sand Coral Beach offers stunning sunset view\r\n\r\n• Natural Bridge: Also known as Howrah Bridge the bridge has naturally formed by corals, its best seen during the low tide.\r\n\r\n• Sightseeing will be based on tide and local representative will brief the final schedule.\r\n\r\n5th Day (Sun 14th August) : Neil Island to Port Blair - Day at Leisure\r\n\r\n• Breakfast, check out and proceed for jetty and onward journey to Port Blair\r\n\r\n• Arrival in Port Blair, Transfer to your booked hotel, Day free for shopping/ leisure.\r\n\r\n• Other places like Corbin’s Cove Beach/ Chidiya Tapu/ Wandoor Beach/ Museums & Parks can be covered at additional cost subject to time and \r\n availability (Optional: at direct payment basis).\r\n\r\n6th Day (Mon 15th August) : Port Blair Departure - Tour Ends\r\n\r\n• Breakfast, Transfer to airport, Tour Ends.\r\n\r\n• Port Blair airport is small with heavy traffic, we recommend you reach the airport at least 2 hrs prior to your flight timing.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','• Return Airfare\r\n\r\n• Transportation\r\n\r\n• Meet & Greet services by our local representatives at Airport & Jetty.\r\n\r\n• Meal Plan – CP (Bed + Breakfast)\r\n\r\n• Airport & Ferry Terminal Transfers in Air-Conditioned Vehicle.\r\n\r\n• All Sightseeing (Entry fess included) as per itinerary in Air-Conditioned Vehicle.\r\n\r\n• Inter-Island Transfers By Private Catamaran Ferries Makruzz/ Nautika/ Green Ocean/ ITT Majestic etc (Subject to Availability)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nTransportation\r\n\r\n1 Xylo / Ertiga\r\n\r\n 1st Day (10 Aug) Port Blair Arrival - Cellular Jail – Light & Sound Show\r\n\r\n 2nd Day (11 Aug) Port Blair to Havelock - Radha Nagar Beach\r\n\r\n 3rd Day (12 Aug) Havelock - Elephenta Beach\r\n\r\n 4th Day (13 Aug) Havelock to Neil Island - Laxmanpura Beach, Bharatpura Beach & \r\n   Natural Bridge\r\n\r\n 5th Day (14 Aug) Neil Island to Port Blair - Day at Leisure\r\n\r\n 6th Day (15 Aug)	Port Blair Departure - Tour Ends\r\n\r\n','• The services of vehicles not on disposal basis & finishing the sightseeing tour as per the itinerary\r\n\r\n• Any kind of personal expenses or optional tours/extra meals/ Vehicle for Dinner etc.\r\n\r\n•  Anything not in inclusions is excluded\r\n','','2022-08-10','2022-08-15',1,0,0,'2022-07-27 19:04:11','2022-07-27 19:32:35'),(148,440,349,2,0,0,25800,3000,'Amazing Dubai','No of Pax : 02\r\n\r\nCheck In : 10/08/2022\r\n\r\nCheck Out : 14/08/2022\r\n\r\nNationality : Indian\r\n\r\nDestination : Dubai','','Return airport transfers on Pvt\r\n\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\n\r\nDesert safari with dinner on sic\r\n\r\nDhow cruise creek with dinner on sic\r\n\r\nDubai half day city tour on sic\r\n\r\nAbudhabi City tour\r\n\r\nBurj khalifa 124 floor no. Prime time on sic','Anything which is not included in inclusions.','','2022-08-10','2022-08-14',1,0,0,'2022-08-01 19:56:07','2022-08-01 20:19:07'),(149,449,507,2,1,0,0,0,'Scenic Nepal',' Package itinerary\r\n06 Sep. 2022:\r\n* Pickup from Kathmandu International Airport & drop at hotel.\r\n* Welcome drink at hotel.\r\n* Dinner at hotel.\r\n* Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\r\n07 Sep. 2022:\r\n* Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Full day Sightseeing in Kathmandu covering Pasupatinath, Bauddhanath Stupa, Swyambhunath (Monkey Temple) & Kathmandu Durbar Square.\r\n* Dinner at hotel.\r\n* Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\r\n08 Sep. 2022:\r\n* Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Drive from Kathmandu to Pokhara via Manakamana Temple Darshan (Cable Car) & drop at hotel.   210 KM   (6-7 Hours)\r\n* Dinner at hotel.\r\n* Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.\r\n09 Sep. 2022:\r\n* Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Full day sightseeing in Pokhara covering Bindabashini Temple, Gupteshor Cave, Devi;s  Fall,  Phewa Lake, Seti Gorge & Peace Pagoda.\r\n* Dinner at hotel..\r\n* Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.\r\n10 Sep. 2022:\r\n* Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Drive from Pokhara to Kathmandu & drop at hotel.   210 KM  (6-7 Hours)\r\n* Dinner at hotel.\r\n* Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\r\n11 Sep. 2022:\r\n* Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Drive from hotel to Kathmandu International airport.\r\n','','•	Welcome soft drink.\r\n•	Airport pickup & drop with a/c Sedan Car\r\n•	Kathmandu one full day sightseeing.\r\n•	03 night’s accommodation at respective hotel in Kathmandu with MAP Plan. \r\n•	02 night’s accommodation at respective hotel in Pokhara with MAP Plan. \r\n•	Pokhara full day sightseeing.\r\n','• Monuments and museum entrance fees for above sightseeing places.\r\n• Manakamana Cable Car Ticket Cost INR. 550/= Per Person.\r\n','','2022-09-06','2022-09-11',1,0,0,'2022-08-05 01:03:48','2022-08-05 01:03:48'),(150,454,15530,2,0,0,0,0,'Andaman Diaries','Port Blair 1 Night / Havelock 2 Nights / Port Blair 1 Night\r\n\r\n??????? ?????????\r\n\r\n1st Day (Wed 21st September) : Port Blair Arrival - Cellular Jail – Light & Sound Show\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Thu 22nd September) : Port Blair to Havelock - Radha Nagar Beach\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Fri 23rd September) : Havelock - Elephenta Beach\r\n\r\n4th Day (Sat 24th September) : Havelock to Port Blair - Day at Leisure\r\n\r\n5th Day (Sun 25th September) : Port Blair Departure - Tour Ends\r\n\r\n\r\n??????? ???????: 1 Xylo/ Ertiga\r\n','','\r\n• Meet & Greet services by our local representatives at Airport & Jetty.\r\n• Meal Plan – CP (Bed + Breakfast)\r\n• Airport & Ferry Terminal Transfers in Air-Conditioned Vehicle.\r\n• All Sightseeing (Entry fess included) as per itinerary in Air-Conditioned Vehicle.\r\n• Inter-Island Transfers By Private Catamaran Ferries Makruzz/ Nautika/ Green Ocean/ ITT Majestic etc (Subject to Availability)\r\n\r\n','\r\n• The services of vehicles not on disposal basis & finishing the sightseeing tour as per the itinerary\r\n• Any kind of personal expenses or optional tours/extra meals/ Vehicle for Dinner etc.\r\n \r\nAnything not in inclusion is excluded','','2022-09-21','2022-09-25',1,0,0,'2022-08-10 01:22:23','2022-08-10 01:22:23'),(151,456,319,5,2,0,0,0,'Cambodia','No of Adults : 05\r\n\r\nChild : 02 (11,11)\r\n\r\nCheck In : 25/12/2022\r\n\r\nCheck Out : 28/12/2022\r\n\r\nNationality : Indian\r\n\r\nDestination : Cambodia\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrive – Phnom Penh, Sour Sdey “Hello” Cambodia \r\nUpon arrival at Phnom Penh Int’s Airport, process immigration procedure, then get your luggage and walk straight to the Exit Gate where our driver (no guide) is waiting. After self-introduced, you’ll transfer directly around 45 minutes to the hotel in the city for check in (check in time is 2pm). \r\n\r\nVisit to the Royal Palace compound (closed for renovation and reopen on October 2022) build in 1866 by the Predecessors of King Norodom, is the most conspicuous feature and also one of impressive colorful Khmer-style Palaces. Nearside the Royal Palace is Silver Pagoda (The Emerald Buddha temple), display plenty of Buddha Statues that were decorated and made by diamond, emerald, gold and silver. Continue to National Museum, the distinctive red building with a beautiful Khmer architecture was built since 1917 and contains more than 5000 art objects made of sandstone, bronze, silver, copper, wood and others. Next, we head to visit Wat Phnom “Mountain Pagoda” is a Buddhist temple that symbolizes the name of Phnom Penh, located on the hill. According to legend, the first pagoda on this site was erected in 1372 to house four statues of Buddha deposited here by the waters of the Mekong River and discovered by Lady Penh. Wat Phnom is the most popular place for local people come to play healthy spot or praying for their good luck as well as admire the sundown.\r\nOvernight in Phnom Penh.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Phnom Penh – Siem Reap (Meal: Breakfast, Lunch)\r\nAfter breakfast, pick up by driver (no guide) and transfer to Phnom Penh airport for flight to Siem Reap. Upon arrival in Siem Reap airport, meet our guide and transfer to city.\r\n\r\nWe will enjoy a boat ride on the Tonle Sap Lake. This is the largest permanent fresh-water lake in South East Asia and flows into Tonle Sap River, joining the Mekong in Phnom Penh. We will see a fishermen\'s \"floating village\" with floating schools, floating police station, etc. It is same as a big village floating on the lake, and the \"village\" move from place-to-place following water levels and current. And then ARTISAN D’ANGKOR has developed from the ambitious belief that it is possible to revive ancient Khmer Arts & Crafts while improving the lives of thousands of people living in rural areas.\r\nOvernight in Siem Reap.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Angkor Highlight (Meal: Breakfast, Lunch)\r\nEnjoy breakfast at hotel.\r\n\r\nWe drive to Angkor Thom that was the masterpiece of King Jayavarman VII. Following the occupation of Angkor by the Chams from 1177 to 1181, the new king decided to build an impregnable fortress at the heart of his empire. \r\n\r\nWe begin to visit Bayon Temple. At the exact center of Angkor Thom, this is an eccentric expression of the creative genius and inflated ego of Cambodia’s most celebrated king.\r\nPhoto stop at Terrace of the Leper King. Along the Terrace of Elephants, originally used as a viewing gallery for the king to preside over parades, performances and traditional sports. At the southern end lies the Baphuon, once of the most beautiful temples at Angkor, dating from the reign of Uditayavarman 1 in the 11th century.\r\n\r\nVisit the picturesque Ta Prohm that had nearly disappeared into the jungle and remains overgrown, an oddly haunting and exotic scene. The magnificent roots of a tree, pushing between the huge stone blocks of the temple in a sort of embrace, evoke feelings that you may remember forever.\r\n\r\nWe journey out to the mother of all temples, Angkor Wat. Believed to be the world\'s largest religious building, this temple is the perfect fusion of symbolism and symmetry and a source of pride and strength to all Khmers. \r\nOvernight in Siem Reap.\r\n\r\nInclusion: Transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, breakfast and hotel & lunch\r\n\r\nDay 4: Siem Reap – Departure (Meal: Breakfast)\r\nTransfer to Siem Reap airport for departure to next destination. It’s time to say goodbye, we thank you for traveling with us and warmly welcome you to come again. \r\n\r\nInclusion: Transfer, guide, water and breakfast\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','•Accommodation with daily breakfast in double / twin / triple shared room\r\n\r\n•Meal: 2 Lunches (Set Menu and foods only) at local restaurant as mention in program (B: Breakfast, L: Lunch and D: Dinner)\r\n\r\n•Airport transfers & Tours by air con. vehicles as per program\r\n\r\n•Sightseeing and entrance fees as specified\r\n\r\n•Local English-speaking guide as per program\r\n\r\n•All boat trip as mentioned in program\r\n\r\n•2 bottles of cold water and 2 towel per day\r\n','•Cambodia Visa stamp fee: 30$ (Passport valid more than 6 months, enough space for visa stamp (2 free spaces), 1 passport photo (4X6), cash 30$)\r\n\r\n•All International air tickets\r\n\r\n•Other meal, drink, personal expenses, tip, Travel insurance\r\n\r\n•Another thing not mentioned in included\r\n','','2022-12-25','2022-12-28',0,0,0,'2022-08-11 12:10:24','2022-08-12 13:14:07'),(152,457,38,10,0,0,0,0,'Bangkok, pattaya','No of Pax : 10\r\n\r\nCheck in : 13/09/22\r\n\r\nCheck Out : 19/09/22\r\n\r\nNationality : Indian\r\n\r\nDestination : Bangkok, Pattaya','','Return airfare\r\n\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\n\r\nHalf day BKK temple tour (2 temple) - Pvt transfer\r\n\r\nFull day Safari world + marine park with Lunch - Pvt transfer\r\n\r\nPattaya Coral island tour by speed boat with Lunch - Pvt\r\n\r\nAlcazar show + 1 soft drink (Normal seat) - Pvt\r\n\r\nBKK Airport - Pattaya Hotel - Pvt transfer\r\n\r\nPattaya Hotel - BKK Hotel - PVT transfer\r\n\r\nBKK Hotel - BKK Airport - PVT Transfer\r\n\r\n\r\n','Anythung which is noy included in inclusions.','','2022-09-13','2022-09-19',1,0,0,'2022-08-11 12:44:01','2022-08-11 12:44:01'),(153,455,54,10,0,0,0,0,'Singapore, Malasyia','No of Pax : 10\r\n\r\nCheck in : 13/09/22\r\n\r\nCheck Out : 